crazy, neutral female human Valkyrie


Well, i did this one in 3 days. This is one of the fastest games i
have played in real time and in turns used . (32755) This was fast
for me, but there is always room for improvement. 


The game was a standard valk beginning. Just starting whacking things
from the start. I didn't have much choice in the matter since my pet
dog died from a pit on the first couple of turns. 

The DoD was nice to me this game. I had large shops on levels 2-5 and 
an armor store on lvl 9 and general store on lvl 10. There was more
but since i didn't even bother exploring past lvl 14 these are the
only ones that actually helped my game. 

One nice early wand was poly, but since i had no pets this wasn't used
at this point. 

I went to do soko first but i found an altar on lvl c 6 and  found a
bones file lvl 7. This dude had two amulets and one happened to be
reflection. One of the shops on the way gave me a BoH. I hadn't even
done soko or the mines and at this point i was tempted to skip them. 

I made a minor mistake at this point. I went dipping for Excalibur. 
Most of my valks where lawful and didn't realize this one was was
neutral until a got a fountain message i had never seen before.
whoops. 

Did soko and acquired two pets. Used the wand and Maus and Liepling
turned into a golden naga and wood elf. That's good enough for me. 
when i finished soko Maus lvl up into a lord. 


Well, i sorted all my junk and use the altar on lvl 6 to BUC
everything. One of the scrolls was a  blessed id but since i still
had not gotten to mine town i decided to save it for the time being.
I started dipping to uncurse my sword and when that was done i
converted the altar and saced until i got mojo. 

I this point i was at exp lvl 10. To lvl up my buddies and to keep my
exp where it was i stopped killing things. We killed all the
shopkeepers for the dough except for the one tending the general
store on dlvl 2. 

Mine town had no lamps and only 4 candles, but i managed to get naked
ac protection of 3 after my pets killed all the shopkeepers. Then
even though the priest was co-aligned i had him rubbed out too. I
found a lvl 1 spell book and read it so that i could have a means to
become confused. 

I schlepped all the stuff back to my stash on lvl 7. I then went to
get some more stuff from the shops on lvl 9 and 10. I was lucky and
found a magic lamp already blessed. The other blessed potion of water
went to bless my bag. I used the wish for the eye of the tapioca. 

Now i went and used the scroll of id to see what i had for potions and
scrolls and wands. I had 3 wands that disappeared text so i knew i
had cancellation and teleport, but i wasn't prepared for what else i
had. I had a ring of tel control. I had a scroll of teleport that was
already cursed. I had unholy water (i wonder why i didn't notice that
before) and one scroll of genocide and two of charging. Ascending
from this point was just going through the motions. 

I blessed genocided L first chance i got. 

Step one polypile some of this junk. The first step netted me free
action and lev for rings, tools included a magic whistle, lenses and
a tinning kit, and wands included enlightenment and probing. Used the
lenses to read spell books up to level 3. Switched my cloak of
displacement for the robe. 

Second round netted me speed boots. 

Step two was to get holy water. I  canceled scrolls, potions and
cursed items and went to the altar to pray.  

Step three was to get the castle wand. Used the c?oT and went to the
valley. Went up and cleared the castle. Having -17 for ac meant that
i had to use elbereth fighting the dragons but i made it. Only the
white dragon dropped scales.  


I grabbed from the castle  ?,!, +, wands, tools and k-rats. Oh ,and
the castle WoW. Then i went down and cleared the valley. I kept Maus
the elven king and Liepling the Golden Nag  out of harms way while i
went into the thick of things with a ring of conflict. Enough wraiths
dropped corpses to reach lvl 15 

step 4 was to retrieve the luck stone from mines end. I didn't know
the orb of weight provided this service or i would have skipped this
step. I invoked the eye to get to mines end, but since i hadn't
explored deeper than mine town that was where it dropped me off.
Damn, learn something new every game. 

Got the luck stone and did a sac fest until my luck was maxed out. I
think i also got crowned at this point and so switched to vorpal
blade. (i didn't want stuff to blow up.) I had this intention in mind
from the start and never advanced hammer past basic. 

I saw that my spell casting ability at lvl 17 was pretty good so i
used the castle wand (0:3) for a HoB +3. all lvl 2 spells where at 0%
and lv l 3 at unskilled was about 30%. I will take charm monster at
30% any day of the week. Another round of polying after reading all
my spell books, got me an +oID. All the other 6 wishes went to magic
markers. 

I enchanted up my armor, proofed  it, and read charging until my spell
points where up to 200. I had to use 2 or 3 !oB since i went so fast
none of my spells timed out yet. I also enchanted 20 daggers to +6
and vorpy up to +6




Step 4 was to go finish the quest. I zipped through it and tinned
enough giants to get my str up to 18:00. The quest was on lvl 13 and
this is the last level i bothered exploring in the DoD. 

After the quest i use the eye and the orb to get me to the bottom of
Hell. Found the vibrating square and marked it. (lvl 49) Lvl 48
contained the portal so i stepped through it. the bottom of the tower
was on lvl 40. I read MM and cleared the tower . Repeated this for
the next level and on Rodney's lair  MM revealed the fork to Vlad's. 

I invoked the orb again to get me to level 39 and went down to get to
Vlad's. After clearing Vlad's tower i went back to my stash to get
all  my blank scrolls. the last poly session actually created a +of
MM but it was at 80%. Still, it would save me some charges on my
markers. 

I also did my last adjustment of my stash. I cursed all my !ofGl and
used alchemy to turn 9 !ofH into EH. I didn't convert the resulting
potions into full healing because i needed gain level to zip past
hell. I also didn't need the HP that badly. 



I went and killed Rodney and went into the sanctum. I used the trick
of going up and then lvl porting back down to avoid the grave yard. I
was deposited in the big room about 6 steps away from the temple
door. Went in and killed the priest. I found and named the amulet
coke and drank my first c!oGl. 

The next trick was to use the portal on lvl 48 to skip 8 levels on the
run up . (I never even visited lvls  47-41 and all i saw from 37-29
and 26-14 was what was revealed from Magic mapping. ) I used to think
that being in the tower prevented the mysterious force but i was
mistaken. I was thrown back from Rodney lair back to the bottom of
the tower. damn.

When i reached the wizards lair i dropped the amulet and waited until
Maus picked it up. then i invoked the eye to get to Vlad's, stepped
outside, and whistled Maus over. Man i love shortcuts. 

I used controlled teleport the rest of the way up when i could and
c!ofgl when i couldn't.  I ran out of potions after Jubi's swamp and
had to walk past the last demon's lair. I also had to walk past the
castle and killed Medusa as an afterthought in her swamp. 

the rest of the way up was either reading ? of MM or casting it and
then porting to the stairs. When i hit my stash i took 2 blanks spell
books and any scrolls and potions  i had left. I canceled most of
them  and made holy water with the potions. I also made sure to take
some k-rats with me. 

The planes went quick. Even water was quick with the portal floating
towards me once i made it to the middle of the level. Astral was a
pain because i only had two wands of teleport. This on top of the
fact that i had to do the grand tour made it a pain, but only because
i just wanted to sac the amulet and go to bed. 

I always go up the middle first. I Put on a blindfold and found out it
was death. I waited until it stepped next to me and whacked it. Then
i got a free turn and i killed it. This happened with all the riders.
None of them ever got a hit on me. Next i went left and when i
checked it turned out to be pesty. Famine was to the right and once
it went down I teleported all the rest of the rabble out of my way. 




